   "source": [
    "# ML-10 — Content Action Playbook\n",
    "\n",
    "This skeleton is yours to fill. Work the sections **in order** — each one has a one-line hint. Simple words, honest numbers.\n",
    "\n",
    "> Working with an AI assistant? Tell it to read `skills/README.md` first and load the one skill this assignment names on its card."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9240800c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Ranked actions + reason codes\n",
    "\n",
    "Combining two things validated in Weeks 4-6: the Random Forest model's score (precision@50 ≈\n",
    "0.70 on a client-grouped holdout, per Week 6) and a light archetype clustering that groups\n",
    "content into four descriptive segments, each mapped to a different action — not one action for\n",
    "everyone.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Archetypes → actions** (k-means, k=4, on visibility/position/CTR/staleness/depth):\n",
    "\n",
    "| Archetype | n | Profile | Action |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| High-Visibility Decliners | 12,205 | High impressions (8.9K), decent position (16.5), long content, **highest decline rate (60%)** | `refresh_priority` |\n",
    "| Visible but Thin | 9,442 | Moderate impressions (4.9K), weak position (22.1), thinnest content (1.7K words) | `expand_and_refresh` |\n",
    "| Fresh but Low-Reach | 8,194 | Best-ish position (9.6), freshest (22d), but almost no traffic (64 impr) | `monitor_promote` |\n",
    "| Low-Volume Outliers | 159 | Near-zero impressions (4.6), oddly high CTR — small-sample noise | `exclude_low_confidence` |\n",
    "\n",
    "The last row matters as much as the first: 159 items look \"great\" on CTR alone, but at n≈5\n",
    "impressions each, that CTR is statistical noise, not signal — the honest move is to exclude\n",
    "them from automated scoring rather than let a tiny denominator produce a false top-of-queue\n",
    "pick."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "d81c9d93",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-16T07:29:32.157606Z",
