    "## 2. Intended use and limits\n",
    "\n",
    "**Intended use:** a weekly-review starting point for a content editor on Lane 2 (Refresh /\n",
    "Content Opportunity Scoring), covering the same 32-client, 30,000-item starter dataset used\n",
    "throughout this capstone. It ranks *where to look first*, it does not decide *what to publish*.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Limits, stated plainly:**\n",
    "- The label (`is_declining_label`) is a **proxy** — a rule about recent impression trend, not a\n",
    "  confirmed editorial judgment that a page needs work (established Week 2).\n",
    "- Validated precision (≈0.70 at top-50) comes from **one client-grouped holdout of 6 clients**\n",
    "  (Week 6) — directional, not a guaranteed rate on a different client mix.\n",
    "- The **decay pattern in this dataset runs opposite to FlyRank's own published paper**: here,\n",
    "  decline rate falls as content ages (67% at 0-90d → 43% at 365d+), while the paper reports\n",
    "  content declining *after* 270 days. I'm not resolving that conflict — I'm naming it, because a\n",
    "  playbook that silently picked whichever direction was more convenient would be dishonest. The\n",
    "  likely explanation is that very young pages in this dataset have small impression bases, so a\n",
    "  small absolute drop reads as a large relative \"decline\" — but that's a hypothesis, not a\n",
    "  confirmed cause.\n",
    "- Archetypes are **descriptive groupings from this snapshot**, not fixed permanent categories —\n",
    "  a page's archetype can and will change next month."
   ]
  },
