   "source": [
    "## 3. Human review + the no-go list\n",
    "\n",
    "**A human must check, before acting on any top-ranked item:**\n",
    "- Is a SERP feature (featured snippet, AI Overview, ads) suppressing clicks regardless of\n",
    "  content quality? The model has no visibility into what's on the results page.\n",
    "- Was this page already updated recently, in a way not yet reflected in trend signals? A\n",
    "  refresh already in flight shouldn't be flagged as needing one.\n",
    "- Is the pattern seasonal? A single 90-day window can't distinguish a seasonal dip from a real\n",
    "  decline (named as a limitation back in Week 3).\n",
    "- Is the item in the `exclude_low_confidence` archetype? If so, treat any score for it as noise,\n",
    "  not signal, regardless of how it ranks.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What must NOT be automated:**\n",
    "- No auto-publishing or auto-editing content from this score. Every action is a suggestion for\n",
    "  a human, never an executed change.\n",
    "- No use of this score as a performance measure for a person, a client, or a piece of content in\n",
    "  isolation — it's a proxy-based triage tool, not a quality certification.\n",
    "- No skipping human review for top-ranked items just because they're top-ranked — rank order is\n",
    "  a starting point for attention, not a confidence guarantee.\n",
    "- No applying this playbook to a different lane, client mix, or dataset without re-validating —\n",
    "  the precision numbers are specific to this data, this split, this snapshot.\n",
    "- No treating `is_declining_label` as ground truth anywhere downstream — it's a proxy, stated as\n",
    "  such since Week 2, and that doesn't change just because a model was trained on it."
   ]
  },
