    "## 4. Monitoring / retrain triggers\n",
    "\n",
    "**Cost/value thinking first, since it sets the trigger thresholds:** at precision@50 ≈ 0.70, an\n",
    "editor reviewing the top 50 each week spends time on roughly 15 wasted reviews (false\n",
    "positives) to reach 35 real ones. If precision@50 drifts down toward the dataset's ~54% base\n",
    "rate, the model is adding little over random ranking and the review time stops paying for\n",
    "itself — that threshold is a natural trigger, not an arbitrary one.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Triggers:**\n",
    "- **Precision decay:** recompute precision@50 against realized outcomes each month; if it falls\n",
    "  below roughly 0.55 (close to the base rate), the model has stopped beating a naive rule and\n",
    "  needs retraining or reverting to the Week-4 baseline.\n",
    "- **Feature drift:** track the monthly mean of `impressions_90d` and `avg_position` (the top two\n",
    "  Random Forest features per Week 5); a large shift signals the training data no longer\n",
    "  resembles what's being scored.\n",
    "- **Client mix change:** if the active client count moves meaningfully from 32, archetypes\n",
    "  should be refit — cluster shapes were learned on this specific mix.\n",
    "- **Schedule:** retrain quarterly at minimum regardless of drift, and immediately if the data\n",
    "  contract changes (new/renamed columns, per Week 3's contract)."
   ]
  },
